 "findings": [
  {
   "id": "F1",
   "title": "Legacy startup script times out early",
   "result": "MGS wait limit is about 145-170 s instead of 300 s (loop counts iterations, not seconds); LNET wait about 11 s instead of 60 s."
  },
  {
   "id": "F2",
   "title": "Head-1 (MGS) is always the last node up",
   "result": "Reaches the OS about 190 s after its own power-on versus about 90 s for other blades."
  },
  {
   "id": "F3",
   "title": "Startup fix verified",
   "result": "With wall-clock deadlines computes waited up to 344 s for the MGS (Head-1 held 240 s) and all 10 nodes mounted with 0 fatal retries."
  },
  {
   "id": "F4",
   "title": "Data integrity across unclean power-off",
   "result": "40/40 files sha256-identical after each of 2 hard power-offs of all 10 nodes."
  },
  {
   "id": "F5",
   "title": "OST recovery window after unclean stop",
   "result": "After a hard stop of all nodes only 2 of 16 OSTs were visible for another 275-292 s (5:00 recovery window; MDT with abort_recov is denied as new client). Graceful shutdown: pool complete immediately. Accepted (scheduled shutdowns)."
  },
  {
   "id": "F6",
   "title": "Kernel update would break the boot",
   "result": "dnf update installed Rocky 9.8 kernel on Compute-2, UPDATEDEFAULT=yes made it the default; no Lustre modules on boot. Fixed: kernel* excluded, UPDATEDEFAULT=no."
  },
  {
   "id": "F7",
   "title": "FLR is delayed mirroring",
   "result": "Writes land on one mirror; the other stays stale until lfs mirror resync (stale=12/12 and 20/20 right after writing). Without resync, data on a lost node is unavailable until it returns."
  },
  {
   "id": "F8",
   "title": "Reads fail over automatically when mirrors are in sync",
   "result": "Node loss with resynced mirrors: 246-292 reads ok during a 240 s outage, longest stall 3-41 s, 0 failures after return."
  },
  {
   "id": "F9",
   "title": "Writes and creates block on a dead OSS unless its OSTs are deactivated",
   "result": "Without action: no write completed during the outage, one create blocked 344 s. With the dead OSTs deactivated on MDS+client: 21 writes and 180 creates ok, only the in-flight operations failed (51-57 s); 38/38 written files intact."
  },
  {
   "id": "F10",
   "title": "Metadata is not redundant",
   "result": "New directories alternate between MDT0 and MDT1; losing a head stalls the directories on its MDT (write 240 s, creates failed after 60 s). Head-1 loss also evicts clients on return (abort_recov): first 2 read-backs I/O errors."
  },
  {
   "id": "F11",
   "title": "Rolling reboot can leave a node's IB port in INIT",
   "result": "Loop 1 of 2 passed (10/10). Loop 2: Head-2's port stayed INIT about 10 min (no SM activated it); both head OpenSMs STANDBY; OpenSM runs on all 10 nodes with equal priority. Recovered by restarting OpenSM on Head-1."
  },
  {
   "id": "F12",
   "title": "Deterministic subnet-manager layout fixes the rolling reboot",
   "result": "OpenSM only on the heads (Head-1 priority 14, Head-2 13), off on the computes; reboot.yml waits for the IB port ACTIVE. Rolling reboot repeated: 3 of 3 loops passed (about 1520-1540 s each), pool HEALTHY. Small sample; cause not fully proven (why the previous master did not activate Head-2's port is unexplained)."
  }
